"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[9385],{58481:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"init","desc":"Builds the initial `RouterState` from a flat descriptor list. Called once\\nper `RouterProvider` mount, through the lazy initializer of\\n`React.useReducer`.\\n\\nThree things happen here:\\n\\n1. Descriptors are keyed by `path` into `state.routes`, so declaration\\n   order in `Client.luau` never matters.\\n2. The lone `isDefault` descriptor (if any) becomes the starting\\n   `currentPath`. With no default, `currentPath` starts `nil` and the\\n   route slot renders nothing.\\n3. Every portal descriptor is auto-mounted \u2014 an empty props table is\\n   written into `mountedPortals` unless the descriptor sets\\n   `autoMountPortal = false`.\\n\\nAsserts on a duplicate path, on a portal flagged `isDefault`, and on a\\nsecond default route.","params":[{"name":"routes","desc":"Every route the app can render","lua_type":"{ RouteDescriptor }"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"RouterState"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":133,"path":"src/Client/App/Router/store.luau"}},{"name":"reducer","desc":"Pure state transition. Never mutates `state` \u2014 portal changes clone\\n`mountedPortals` before writing, and every branch that changes something\\nreturns a fresh state table.\\n\\nInvalid transitions `warn` and return the input state untouched:\\n\\n* `navigate` to an unknown path, or to a portal (mount it instead)\\n* `mount` / `unmount` of an unknown path\\n* `unmount` of the default route, which is meant to be the always-rendered\\n  base view\\n\\nTwo conveniences are worth knowing: `mount` on a *regular* route is\\nrewritten into a `navigate`, and `unmount` of a regular route that isn\'t\\nthe current one is a no-op rather than a state reset.","params":[{"name":"state","desc":"Current state","lua_type":"RouterState"},{"name":"action","desc":"Transition to apply","lua_type":"Action"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"RouterState"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":195,"path":"src/Client/App/Router/store.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[{"name":"RouteProps","desc":"Free-form props handed to a route\'s component when it renders. Passed\\nthrough `navigate` / `mount` and stored verbatim in the state \u2014 the Router\\nnever inspects them.","fields":[{"name":"[string]","lua_type":"any","desc":"Whatever the route\'s component expects"}],"source":{"line":18,"path":"src/Client/App/Router/types.luau"}},{"name":"RouteDescriptor","desc":"Declares one route. The full list lives in `src/Client/App/Client.luau`\\nand is handed to `Router.Provider` at mount.\\n\\n`isPortal` is the important flag: portal routes render concurrently in\\ntheir own slots, regular routes share a single mutually-exclusive slot.\\n`isDefault` picks the regular route that is active from the first render\\nand can never be unmounted; it is invalid on a portal.","fields":[{"name":"path","lua_type":"string","desc":"Unique key used to navigate/mount. Duplicates assert at init"},{"name":"component","lua_type":"React.ComponentType<RouteProps>","desc":"Rendered by `Views` with the route\'s props"},{"name":"isDefault","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"Regular routes only. Starts active, cannot be unmounted"},{"name":"isPortal","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"Renders concurrently with the active route and other portals"},{"name":"autoMountPortal","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"Portals only. Set `false` to stay unmounted until asked"}],"source":{"line":38,"path":"src/Client/App/Router/types.luau"}},{"name":"RouterState","desc":"Everything the Router knows, rebuilt on each reducer transition and\\npublished through `Provider.StateContext`.","fields":[{"name":"routes","lua_type":"{ [string]: RouteDescriptor }","desc":"Every declared route, keyed by path"},{"name":"currentPath","lua_type":"string?","desc":"The one active regular route, or nil when the slot is empty"},{"name":"currentProps","lua_type":"RouteProps?","desc":"Props for the active regular route"},{"name":"mountedPortals","lua_type":"{ [string]: RouteProps }","desc":"Path -> props for each concurrently mounted portal"}],"source":{"line":58,"path":"src/Client/App/Router/types.luau"}},{"name":"NavigationApi","desc":"The imperative half of the Router, obtained with `Router.useNavigation()`.\\nEvery method is a `dispatch` wrapper and returns immediately \u2014 the boolean\\nreports that the action was dispatched, not that the transition was valid.\\nRejected transitions surface as a `warn` from the reducer.\\n\\n`navigateToDefault` is the exception: it scans the descriptor list itself\\nand returns `false` when no route is flagged `isDefault`.","fields":[{"name":"navigate","lua_type":"(path: string, props: RouteProps?) -> boolean","desc":"Swap the regular-route slot"},{"name":"mount","lua_type":"(path: string, props: RouteProps?) -> boolean","desc":"Mount a portal (or navigate, for a regular route)"},{"name":"unmount","lua_type":"(path: string) -> boolean","desc":"Unmount a portal, or clear the regular-route slot"},{"name":"navigateToDefault","lua_type":"() -> boolean","desc":"Navigate to the `isDefault` route, if one exists"}],"source":{"line":82,"path":"src/Client/App/Router/types.luau"}},{"name":"Action","desc":"A reducer action. `navigate` swaps the single regular-route slot, `mount`\\nadds a portal to `mountedPortals` (or falls through to `navigate` when the\\npath turns out to be a regular route), and `unmount` removes a portal or\\nclears the regular-route slot.","fields":[{"name":"kind","lua_type":"\\"navigate\\" | \\"mount\\" | \\"unmount\\"","desc":"Which transition to apply"},{"name":"path","lua_type":"string","desc":"Route path the action targets"},{"name":"props","lua_type":"RouteProps?","desc":"Props handed to the route\'s component (not on `unmount`)"}],"private":true,"source":{"line":100,"path":"src/Client/App/Router/store.luau"}}],"name":"Router","desc":"The client\'s UI framework. Every screen in the game is a *route* \u2014 a\\n`RouteDescriptor` naming a path, a React component, and a few flags that\\ndecide how and when that component is rendered.\\n\\nRoutes come in two flavors:\\n\\n* **Regular routes** are mutually exclusive. The reducer keeps a single\\n  `currentPath`, so navigating to `\\"CoinShop\\"` implicitly closes whatever\\n  modal was open before it. These are the shops, the inventory modal, the\\n  daily-rewards modal \u2014 anything that owns the screen while it\'s up.\\n* **Portal routes** (`isPortal = true`) are concurrent. Each lives in its\\n  own slot in `mountedPortals` and is rendered alongside the active regular\\n  route and every other mounted portal. These are the persistent HUD layers\\n  \u2014 Root, Hotbar, Toaster, Dialog, Scoreboard, Vote.\\n\\nPortals auto-mount at init. [Router.init] walks the descriptor list and\\nseeds `mountedPortals` with an entry for every `isPortal` descriptor unless\\nit opts out with `autoMountPortal = false`. In practice this means the HUD\\nis up from the first render and nothing has to explicitly mount it.\\n\\n### Wiring\\n\\n`Client.luau` builds the descriptor list and hands it to `App`, which\\nrenders `Router.Provider`. The Provider calls [Router.init] once through\\n`React.useReducer`, then publishes two contexts: the state and a memoized\\n`NavigationApi` whose methods are thin `dispatch` wrappers. `Views` reads\\nboth contexts through the hooks and renders the active route plus each\\nmounted portal.\\n\\n```\\nClient.luau  --routes--\x3e  App  --\x3e  Router.Provider\\n                                     |- StateContext  (RouterState)\\n                                     `- NavContext    (NavigationApi)\\n                                                  |\\n                                     Views --------\'  renders\\n                                       |- current regular route (0 or 1)\\n                                       `- every mounted portal (0..n)\\n```\\n\\n### Dispatch and subscribe\\n\\nThere is no bespoke store object \u2014 the \\"store\\" is this module\'s pure\\n[Router.reducer] driven by React\'s own `useReducer`. Dispatching an\\n[Action] produces a new `RouterState`, React re-renders the two context\\nproviders, and any component using [Router.useCurrentRoute],\\n[Router.useCurrentRouteProps] or [Router.useMountedPortals] re-renders\\nwith it. Subscription is therefore just context subscription; there is\\nnothing to disconnect.\\n\\nThe reducer is deliberately forgiving: unknown paths, navigating to a\\nportal, and unmounting the default route all `warn` and return the state\\nunchanged rather than erroring. [Router.init] is the strict half \u2014 it\\nasserts on duplicate paths, on a portal marked `isDefault`, and on more\\nthan one default route.\\n\\n### Navigating\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal Router = require(ReplicatedFirst.App.Router)\\n\\nlocal function SomeButton()\\n\\tlocal nav = Router.useNavigation()\\n\\n\\treturn e(\\"TextButton\\", {\\n\\t\\t[React.Event.Activated] = function()\\n\\t\\t\\tnav.navigate(\\"CoinShop\\", { tab = \\"gems\\" })\\n\\t\\tend,\\n\\t})\\nend\\n```\\n\\nCopyright (c) 2026 firebit. All rights reserved.\\nfirebit/murder-escape - proprietary and confidential.","realm":["Client"],"source":{"line":79,"path":"src/Client/App/Router/store.luau"}}')}}]);